Package: oneplus-erhai-otg
Version: 1.4
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Description: ADSP OTG host touch for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 On this ADSP firmware the Type-C CC attach detection stays dead after a
 USB-C host session ends (replugs are invisible until reboot). The kernel
 keeps the OTG session armed through detach, so its own self-heal paths are
 off and a plain re-arm is a no-op. This package ships
 /usr/local/sbin/erhai-otg-rearm.sh, a oneshot systemd unit and a udev rule
 set that drive the two steps which actually work (measured 2026-10-28):
 on the detach edge set the dwc3 data role back to host -- that makes the
 ADSP announce the next partner again -- and on the typec partner add event
 turn VBUS on for a sink partner (the kernel's own VBUS write does not
 take). No polling: everything is udev / systemd triggered.
 Requires the erhai kernel (erhai_otg_glink + debugfs).
